{"schema_version":2,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:24-9","provision":"BCO 24-9","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"24-9","title":"Section 24-9","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/24-9/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/24-9","current_text":{"html":"<p>When a ruling elder or deacon cannot or does not for a period of one year perform the duties of his office, his official relationship shall be dissolved by the Session and the action reported to the congregation.</p>","text":"When a ruling elder or deacon cannot or does not for a period of one year perform the duties of his office, his official relationship shall be dissolved by the Session and the action reported to the congregation."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"edce8a8dcd9ced63bb585bf922e6a97319ef62e1","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"f8bde72b35f9475713a5751081d525f119bc6b4daf3b43ddc86694065015654b","parent_id":"bco:24","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records","recommendations":{"status":"incomplete","note":"Recommendation and study papers are not comprehensively indexed by provision."},"history":"partial"},"relationship_count":14,"relationships":[{"id":"bco:24-9--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga43_2015__ci02.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga43_2015__ci02.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Mandating That Those Without Call Report Annually to Presbytery","year":2015,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga43_2015__ci02.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga43_2015__ci02.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga43_2015__ci02.md:occ-e28c0605e15b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga43_2015__ci02.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga43_2015__ci02.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"An overture mandating annual presbytery reporting for officers without call was in conflict with the Constitution because the new BCO 34-10 language conflicted with BCO 42-2.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga43_2015__ci02.md"}]},{"id":"bco:24-9--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga32_2004__ci04.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga32_2004__ci04.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Limit Voting in Presbytery and General Assembly to Pastors and Associate Pastors","year":2004,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga32_2004__ci04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga32_2004__ci04.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga32_2004__ci04.md:occ-87f68de8dbea","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga32_2004__ci04.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga32_2004__ci04.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB again found the overture in conflict with BCO 3-1 and 14-2, reaffirming that restricting voting to pastors disenfranchises non-pastor Teaching Elders.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga32_2004__ci04.md"}]},{"id":"bco:24-9--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga31_2003__ci09.md","record_id":"ccb_advice:inquiries/ga31_2003__ci09.md","type":"CCB advice","title":"Limit Voting in Presbytery and General Assembly to Pastors and Associate Pastors","year":2003,"disposition":"in conflict","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga31_2003__ci09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga31_2003__ci09.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--ccb_advice:inquiries/ga31_2003__ci09.md:occ-eff3fedfa3bb","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga31_2003__ci09.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga31_2003__ci09.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB found the overture in conflict with BCO 3-1, which vests church power in the whole body, and BCO 14-2, which entitles all TEs to representation.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga31_2003__ci09.md"}]},{"id":"bco:24-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Whether \"Inactive Elders\" or Ruling Elders Elected at a Different Church May Serve as Commissioners at General Assembly","year":2014,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md:occ-607b0ed7be18","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"A rotating-session inactive elder may be elected GA commissioner, but a ruling elder never elected in that congregation may not serve as its commissioner.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga42_2014__ci05.md"}]},{"id":"bco:24-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga15_1987__ci04.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga15_1987__ci04.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Emeritus officers voting in higher courts and local bodies","year":1987,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga15_1987__ci04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga15_1987__ci04.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga15_1987__ci04.md:occ-273efc22a06d","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga15_1987__ci04.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga15_1987__ci04.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB affirmed that an Elder Emeritus may not vote in the local session but may vote as a delegate to Presbytery if appointed to serve there.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga15_1987__ci04.md"}]},{"id":"bco:24-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md","record_id":"inquiry:inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md","type":"Constitutional inquiry","title":"Voting rights of Elders and Deacons Emeriti after BCO 24-9 amendment","year":1985,"disposition":"advice given","authority_weight":"medium","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md","evidence_basis":"structured_provision_tag","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--inquiry:inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md:occ-3c27ed21105b","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.html","repository_path":"inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"The CCB noted that the Twelfth GA amended BCO 24-9 to prohibit Emeriti from voting, while a grandfather clause preserved prior voting privileges for those already holding them.","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/inquiries/ga13_1985__ci09.md"}]},{"id":"bco:24-9--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Bowen v. Eastern Carolina Presbytery","year":1991,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--case:cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md:occ-847ead965693","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga19_1991__1990-08.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["infant baptism","limited atonement","fundamentals of the system of doctrine","officer ordination","annulment of ordination","rescinding prior actions","subscription to confessional standards","ruling elder qualification","deacon qualification","covenant theology","TULIP","five points of Calvinism","original jurisdiction","suspension from office without due process","Robert's Rules rescind motion"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1990-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Bowen challenged Presbytery’s attempt, two years after installation, to rescind its earlier ruling and annul local officers’ elections and ordinations without trial. The SJC sustained the complaint: ordination is perpetual, deposition requires judicial process, and rescission was out of order after implementation; Presbytery likewise could not suspend a local elder without due process. But it affirmed that infant baptism and limited atonement are fundamentals admitting no officer exception. The officers remained in office but doctrinally out of accord; voluntary demission or proper process was advised."}},{"id":"bco:24-9--overture:ga43_2015:8","record_id":"overture:ga43_2015:8","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 13-2, 34-10, 24-7 and 24-9 Regarding Ministers, Ruling Elders, and Deacons Without Call","year":2015,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga43_2015.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga43_2015.md","evidence_basis":"title_subject_reference","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--overture:ga43_2015:8:occ-f2a67644b1c5","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga43_2015.html#ga43-p612","repository_path":"markdown/ga43_2015.md#ga43-p612","locator":{"fragment":"ga43-p612","page":612},"excerpt":"Amend BCO 13-2, 34-10, 24-7 and 24-9 Regarding Ministers, Ruling Elders, and Deacons Without Call","sources":[],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga43_2015.md"}],"metadata":{"source":"OVERTURE 8 from Tidewater Presbytery (to CCB, OC)"}},{"id":"bco:24-9--overture:ga32_2004:6","record_id":"overture:ga32_2004:6","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 13-1, 14-2, 23-2, 24-9 to Restrict Voting TEs to Pastors and Associate Pastors","year":2004,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga32_2004.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/markdown/ga32_2004.md","evidence_basis":"title_subject_reference","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:24-9--overture:ga32_2004:6:occ-25019ee24b73","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/markdown/ga32_2004.html#ga32-p157","repository_path":"markdown/ga32_2004.md#ga32